  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "4.1.0 (minor, non-breaking): workspace support. Every business/service call can now be scoped to a workspace (per-project document container) via the X-Workspace-Id header: set EcmSdkOptions.DefaultWorkspaceId (config key Ecm:DefaultWorkspaceId) for a static default, replace IEcmWorkspaceContext to resolve the workspace per request/tenant, or set the new per-request WorkspaceId on DocumentUploadRequest/DocumentBatchUploadRequest/DocumentListQuery (per-request wins over ambient over default). New IEcmClient.Workspaces surface (IWorkspaceClient: ListAsync, FindBySlugAsync) reads the gateway's api/workspaces so integrations can resolve their workspace by slug instead of hard-coding ids. DocumentDto now exposes WorkspaceId (null for legacy/unassigned documents). New shared contract FoxTS.Ecm.Sdk.Contracts.Workspaces.WorkspaceDto. Unset workspace = org-wide (pre-workspace behaviour); no breaking changes.\n\n4.0.0 (packaging): the shared contracts assembly (FoxTS.Ecm.Sdk.Contracts) is now BUNDLED inside this package instead of being shipped as a separate NuGet package. There is a single package to install. The contract types and their FoxTS.Ecm.Sdk.Contracts.* namespaces are unchanged, so source code does not need to change — but if you previously referenced the FoxTS.Ecm.Sdk.Contracts package explicitly (e.g. a transitive pin), remove that reference. No public API changes vs 3.0.0.\n\n3.0.0 (breaking): redesigned client surface. New IEcmClient facade with resource clients (Documents, Tags, TagManagement, Acl, Lookups, TaggingRules, Outbox). Document API is document-id-centric: DownloadAsync(documentId, versionId?), GetViewerUrl, and GetDownloadUrlAsync (server-issued presigned URL) replace the removed version-keyed download/delete/url methods. Tags split by actor: Tags (user self-service, namespace optional - defaults to your personal namespace) vs TagManagement (admin, explicit namespace required, plus namespace CRUD). New ILookupClient (GetDocumentTypesAsync, ResolveUserAsync). IEcmUserContext is now async (GetUserKeyAsync). Multi-targets net8.0 and net10.0. AddEcmSdkClients() enables deferred/hot-reload configuration. Typed DocumentPermission ACL accessors (GetPermissions).",
